@narrator 00:36:31
Future was finally ready for his third album, the record that would not only become his best project, but also be considered one of the most important albums in modern rap history. It was time for Future's grand entrance to the mainstream. As the wave of mainstream pop trap was beginning to rise, with artists like Metro Boomin, the Migos and Young Thug, he wasn't going to get left behind, but he still needed a masterpiece to make it happen. DS2 was the perfection of his sound, and it came at the perfect moment. The first song, "Thought It Was a Drought," starts off with an intoxicating, menacing instrumental. You can hear him shaking the cup of lean, just like you could on Dirty Sprite back in 2011.

@narrator 00:37:22
